15 USC 1681b Permissible Purpose of Consumer Reports This section outlines who can access your credit report and under what circumstances. It requires that anyone who obtains your credit report must have a permissible purpose. 

15 USC 1681c Requirements Relating to Information Contained in Consumer Reports This section specifies what information can and can not be included in your credit report, including the timeframes for how long certain information can remain on your report. 

15 USC 1681e Compliance Procedures This section mandates that credit reporting agencies maintain procedures to ensure the accuracy and integrity of the information contained in consumer reports. 

15 USC 1681i Procedure in Case of Disputed Accuracy This section details the process for disputing inaccuracies on your credit report, including the requirement for credit reporting agencies to investigate disputes. 

15 USC 1681j National Consumer Reporting Agencies This section addresses the responsibilities of national credit reporting agencies to provide you with information about your credit file and the right to receive a free copy of your report under certain conditions. 

15 USC 1681m Requirements on Users of Consumer Reports This section requires users of consumer reports to provide notice when they take adverse action based on information in the report, such as denying credit or employment. 

15 USC 1681n Civil Liability for Willful Noncompliance This section provides for civil liability if a credit reporting agency willfully fails to comply with the requirements of the FCRA. 

