10092178,2024-09-11,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"On XX/XX/22, I discovered that RESERGENT CAPITAL SERVICES conducted an unauthorized soft inquiry on my credit report without my consent or a permissible purpose, as required under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), 15 U.S.C. 1681b. 

I did not apply for any credit or services from XXXX XXXX XXXX, nor did I authorize them to access my credit report in any manner, including through a soft inquiry. Under the FCRA, a company may only obtain a consumers credit report for specific purposes, such as when the consumer applies for credit or if they have a legitimate business need related to a transaction initiated by the consumer. XXXX XXXX XXXX did not meet any of these criteria, and therefore, this inquiry constitutes a violation of my rights under the FCRA. 

While this was a soft inquiry and did not directly impact my credit score, the unauthorized access to my private credit information is a violation of federal law and an infringement on my privacy. 

Relevant Laws : 15 U.S.C. 1681b ( FCRA ) : This section of the FCRA outlines the permissible purposes for which a company can access a consumers credit report. The law specifies that a credit report, even for soft inquiries, can only be obtained for certain legitimate purposes. 
15 U.S.C. 1681n : This section provides for statutory damages of up to {$1000.00} per violation for willful non-compliance with the FCRA, even if no actual damage occurred.",,Resurgent Capital Services L.P.,MD,21218,,Web,2024-09-11,Closed with explanation,Yes
