Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), I have the right to dispute inaccurate information on my credit report, and it is the responsibility of the credit bureau to conduct a reasonable investigation and provide all relevant information used to verify the accuracy of the reporting. 

Please note the following consumer rights that apply to my dispute : Section 611 of the FCRA ( 15 U.S. Code 1681i ) - This section outlines my right to dispute inaccurate information and your obligation to perform a reasonable reinvestigation within 30 days of receiving the dispute. It also requires that I be provided with the results of the investigation, including all supporting evidence. 
Section 609 of the FCRA ( 15 U.S. Code 1681g ) - I have the right to request all information that you have in your file regarding the disputed account, including the identity of anyone who has accessed my credit report and any documents you used to validate the disputed information.

Section 623 of the FCRA ( 15 U.S. Code 1681s-2 ) - Creditors are prohibited from reporting inaccurate information to the credit bureaus. They must also investigate disputes and provide accurate updates to credit bureaus if their reporting is found to be incorrect. 
I respectfully request that you provide me with the requested information and documents as soon as possible. If you fail to provide sufficient evidence supporting the accuracy of the 30-day late payment, I expect the incorrect information to be removed from my credit report immediately. 

