10164742,2024-09-18,Mortgage,FHA mortgage,Struggling to pay mortgage,Foreclosure,"I am writing to formally lodge a complaint against Planet Home Lending , LLC regarding predatory lending practices I have experienced. 

Summary of Complaint I believe that Planet Home Lending has engaged in practices that violate my rights as a borrower, specifically under the Truth in Lending Act ( 15 U.S.C. 1601 et seq. ), the Real Estate Settlement Procedures Act ( 12 U.S.C. 2601 et seq. ), and the Home Ownership and Equity Protection Act ( 15 U.S.C. 1602 ). 

Details of the Complaint Misleading Terms : I was not adequately informed about the true costs of my mortgage, including hidden fees that were not disclosed at the time of signing. 

Excessive Fees : I have been charged fees that appear to be excessive and not in line with industry standards, which I believe are a form of predatory lending. 

Lack of Communication : My attempts to seek clarification and resolve these issues with Planet Home Lending have been met with inadequate responses and a lack of transparency. 

Aside from this, Planet Home Lending has stated that they are now in the process of moving towards foreclosure of my home. I disagree with this action based on an alleged debt, evidenced by a promissory note which I assert is improperly classified due to its negotiable instrument characteristics. 

The note contains language such as "" pay to the order of, '' indicating it is a draft, not a promissory note. An instrument containing an order to pay is not a promissory note. 

Proof : XXXX XXXX ( XXXX ) ; "" XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX 

There is a Lack of Proof of Debt : The lender has not provided adequate proof that the note is a valid promissory note as previously requested. 
Proof : The burden of proof lies with Planet Home Lending. 

Improper Use of Financial Instruments : The note 's characteristics make it ineligible to be used as evidence of debt. 
Proof : XXXX XXXX ( XXXX ) ; Federal Reserve Act, Section 16 ( 38 Stat. 265 ) The terms of the promissory note are unconscionable and unenforceable. 
Proof : Principles of contract law and fairness. 

Planet Home Lending does not have the right or the authority to foreclose on my home. I have filed form XXXX with the IRS revoking their POA via certified mail # XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX on XX/XX/XXXX. This revocation of POA was also recorded with the XXXX XXXX in my countXXXX on XXXX also submitted notice of revocation of POA to Planet via certified mail # XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I received a notice of default and intent to accelerate from Planet Home Lending. On XX/XX/XXXX, I responded with my notice of acceptance via certified mail # XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. In that notice, I requested that the letter be exchanged for discharge after validating the alleged debt. I requested that original documents be returned to me to include the wet ink signature of the promissory note. 

I received correspondence back on XX/XX/XXXX that included copies of the draft that read as a negotiable instrument, and copies of the loan origination documents. 

This was not the debt validation that I requested, as I asked for the wet ink signature of the promissory note to include the deed of trust. I received a copy of a draft and not a promissory note. 

UCC 9-102 ( 65 ) : Defines a promissory note and excludes instruments with orders to pay.

UCC 3-104 ( e ) : Clarifies that an instrument containing an order to pay is a draft.

Restatement of Contracts 2 and 3 : Establishes that a draft can not be utilized as evidence of an outstanding debt. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I submitted a security instrument via registered mail # XXXX in the amount of {$15000.00}. This security instrument was deemed to be tendered for payment per the UCC 3-603. The security instrument was also submitted with a notice of interest to claim letter detailing specific instructions pursuant to the Trust Indenture Act of XXXX. 

