10279603,2024-09-30,Debt collection,I do not know,False statements or representation,Attempted to collect wrong amount,"This letter serves as a formal request for validation of the debt as required under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ) and the Uniform Commercial Code ( UCC ). 

Under 15 U.S.C. 1692g ( b ) of the FDCPA, I have the right to request full verification of this debt. Until proper validation is provided, you are not authorized to pursue collection activities or report this account to credit reporting agencies. Additionally, under 15 U.S.C. 1692e, it is a violation of federal law for a debt collector to make false or misleading representations about the debt.

Information I Require for Debt Validation : Proof that you own the debt or are authorized to collect it on behalf of the original creditor : Under UCC Article 9, specifically UCC 9-404, any assignment of a debt must be properly documented, and I have the right to request evidence of the assignment. Without clear documentation that the debt has been properly assigned to your agency, you are not legally authorized to collect it or report it to credit bureaus. 

Complete payment history and a copy of the original signed contract : To ensure that this debt is valid, I request that you provide the original agreement that created the debt, including my signature, under 15 U.S.C. 1692g ( a ). This is necessary to confirm the legitimacy and accuracy of the debt being collected.

